<title>Video Statement</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
Video <arg>video_name</arg>;
</logicsyntax>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <logiccolor>Video</logiccolor> statement creates a <link Video.csdoc>Video</link> object with the name <arg>video_name</arg>. The Video name must be unique and must contain only letters, numbers, or the underscore character. The name must begin with a letter. You can declare Video objects globally in <logiccolor>PROC GLOBAL</logiccolor> or locally in functions or procedures.


<subheader>Variable Modifiers</subheader>

The following variable modifiers apply to Video objects:

<list>
    <li><logiccolor>persistent</logiccolor>: to persist the variable's value from one run of an application to another.</li>
</list>


